---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const updated = '3 September 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Use"
  description="The terms covering use of this passport photo tool, including what it does, what it cannot guarantee, and the limits of our liability."
>
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink-900">Terms of Use</h1>
  <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-400">Last updated {updated}</p>

  <div class="markdown mt-8 max-w-2xl">
    <h2>What this site provides</h2>
    <p>
      This site provides a free tool that crops and formats a photograph to the published
      specification for a passport, visa or similar document, and summarises those published
      specifications. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by or acting on behalf of any
      government, passport authority, embassy or consulate.
    </p>

    <h2>Accuracy, and what we cannot promise</h2>
    <p>
      The measurements on each page are transcribed from the official source linked at the
      bottom of that page, and each carries the date a person last checked it. Requirements
      do change, and specifications are sometimes interpreted differently by different
      offices handling the same application.
    </p>
    <p>
      We therefore cannot guarantee that a photograph produced here will be accepted. The
      tool reports whether the output meets the measurements we hold on file; acceptance is
      the decision of the authority receiving your application, and factors it judges by eye
      — expression, lighting, shadows on your face, whether your hair covers your eyes — are
      outside what any automated check can confirm. Always read the authority's own page
      before you submit, and treat the linked source as authoritative over this site.
    </p>

    <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>
      Use the tool for your own photographs, or for photographs you have permission to
      process. Do not use it to produce images intended to misrepresent someone's identity,
      and do not attempt to interfere with the site's operation or with other visitors' use
      of it.
    </p>

    <h2>Liability</h2>
    <p>
      The tool is provided as is, without warranty of any kind. To the fullest extent the
      law allows, we are not liable for any loss arising from use of this site, including a
      rejected application, a missed appointment, a delayed trip, or fees you paid to an
      authority. Nothing in these terms limits liability that cannot lawfully be limited.
    </p>

    <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
    <p>
      The text, design and code of this site belong to its operator. Your photographs remain
      entirely yours; we neither receive nor claim any rights in them.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      These terms may be updated, and the date above will change when they are. Continuing
      to use the site after a change means you accept the revised terms.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
